--TEST--
`implements I by $field;` refuses a `$field` that cannot answer `I`, and every member the delegation does not supply is owed as usual — `rule:classes/delegation-by-field`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:classes/delegation-by-field` bullet 1: the delegate has to be a declared property whose
// type is a non-nullable class or interface that satisfies the delegated
// interface. Each half below is a failure the synthesized forward has no
// answer for — no slot to read, no class to dispatch on, or no member to land
// on — and unrefused each one reached `nvs_runtime::nvs_abstract_method`, a
// FATAL naming a compiler bug for what is a mistake in the program.
//
// The whole file is one compile, and every refusal is reported, so a shape
// that stops refusing shows up as a missing line rather than as a plausible
// answer below it.
interface Greets {
    public function greet(): string;
}

interface Counts {
    public function count(): int;
}

final class Polite implements Greets {
    public function greet(): string { return "hi"; }
}

// No property of that name at all.
final class NoField implements Greets by $missing {
}

// Nullable: the forward dispatches on the field at every call, and `null`
// names no class to dispatch on.
final class Maybe implements Greets by $voice {
    private ?Greets $voice;
    public function constructor(?Greets $voice) { $this->voice = $voice; }
}

// A scalar names no members at all.
final class Scalar implements Greets by $voice {
    private string $voice = "x";
}

// A class type that is simply not related to the delegated interface.
final class Unrelated implements Greets by $voice {
    private Counts $voice;
    public function constructor(Counts $voice) { $this->voice = $voice; }
}

// The half the whole-class exemption used to swallow: a class delegating one
// interface is still judged, member by member, on every other interface it
// claims. `Counts::count` is owed here and no forward supplies it.
final class Half implements Greets by $voice, Counts {
    private Greets $voice;
    public function constructor(Greets $voice) { $this->voice = $voice; }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/interfaces
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0720]: `NoField` delegates `Greets` to `$missing`, which is not a property
%A
error[E0720]: `$voice` is `null|Greets`, which cannot satisfy `Greets`
%A
error[E0720]: `$voice` is `string`, which cannot satisfy `Greets`
%A
error[E0720]: `$voice` is `Counts`, which cannot satisfy `Greets`
%A
error[E0449]: `Half` does not declare `count`, which `Counts` requires
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
